Provenance — the implementation itself
--------------------------------------

Unchanged and unaffected by the above. `brotli` is a clean-room pure-Zig
implementation from RFC 7932 ("Brotli Compressed Data Format"). The decoder,
encoder, bit reader, Huffman machinery and command decoding are original Zig; no
reference implementation's source (google/brotli or any other) was ported or
read while implementing. The google/brotli C library was additionally run as a
black-box oracle to cross-check decoded output.

Embedded normative constants
----------------------------

`src/dictionary.bin` (the 122,784-byte static dictionary word list), the context
lookup table, the 121 transforms and the prefix/suffix pool are the **normative
constants of RFC 7932** (Appendices A / B / C). They are, by construction,
byte-identical to those distributed by the google/brotli project, because both
reproduce the same IETF-specified constants — RFC 7932 is a public IETF
specification and these tables are functional data dictated by the format
(merger doctrine; see CONVENTIONS.md §5). The copyright notice above covers them
as well, so the question of whether they are independently copyrightable does
not need to be answered here.
